0..78 Comment "// An eliminator that writes its answer, `if c -> C { … }` or `case e -> C {"
79..158 Comment "// … }`, answers it wherever it stands: the case is ascribed the answer, so a"
159..235 Comment "// computation a `run` binds, which states no type, synthesises it, and each"
236..289 Comment "// arm is checked against it (#2089). The rule is the"
290..360 Comment "// annotation rule of bidirectional typing (Dunfield and Krishnaswami,"
361..431 Comment "// \"Bidirectional Typing\", ACM Computing Surveys 54(5), 2021, § 3: an"
432..478 Comment "// annotated term synthesises its annotation)."
